Language English
Debug Off

Book Basement Ordered No Keep Looped

	Page PlaceStart
		Triggered By @ExploreBasementViaDiningRoom When basementPhase = unlocked
		
		Prolog """
			The basement is so dark you cannot see your hand when you put it 
			through the doorway. An investigator with a light source can go
			into the basement.
		"""
		Button "Enter basement"
		
		Remove TokenExploreBasementViaDiningRoomSight
		Add TileBasement, TokenBasementWall!
		
		TEXT """
			The basement is dark, even with your light. Place the
			{c:TileBasement} tile and wall as indicated, then remove this
			Sight token.
		"""
	End Page PlaceStart

	Page PlaceDarkness
		Add TokenBasementDarkness1!
		Add TokenBasementDarkness2!
		Add TokenBasementDarkness3!
		Add TokenBasementDarkness4!
		
		TEXT """
			Even with a candle, it is dark in the basement. Place Darkness in
			each space of the basement. Investigators can only move into the
			basement when a Light Source is present. The darkness feeds on your
			light:  your Light Source does not cancel the effects of darkness,
			but at least you can see into the room.
		"""
	End Page PlaceDarkness

	Page PlaceEvidence
		Add TokenSearchBasementEvidence!
		
		Text """
			There is a pile of odds and ends near the stairs to your right.
			Place a Search token as indicated.
		"""
	End Page PlaceEvidence

	Page PlaceExploreDungeonCaveViaBasement
		Visible When readAboutExploreDungeonCaveViaBasement
		Triggered By @ReadAboutExploreDungeonCaveViaBasement When exploredBasement And readAboutExploreDungeonCaveViaBasement And Not placedBasementDoor
		
		Add TokenSearchBasementTrapdoor!
		
		Text """
			A stack of boxes sits in the corner of the basement. <i>Is that the
			door we read about in the journal?</i> you consider.

			Place a Search token as indicated.
		"""
		
		If exploredBasement Then Text """
			You remember seeing a stack of boxes in the far corner of the
			basement. <i>Maybe there is a door is behind them,</i> you think to
			yourself.
			
			Place a Search token as indicated.
		"""
		
		placedBasementDoor = true
		
		// if this is set, we must have triggered this page
		If exploredBasement Then Exit
	End Page PlaceExploreDungeonCaveViaBasement
	
	Page PlaceEnd No Text
		exploredBasement = true
		If moveAfterExplore Then Trigger @MoveAfterExplore
		moveAfterExplore = false
		Exit
	End Page PlaceEnd
	
	
	Page SearchEvidence
		Not Visible
		Triggered By @SearchBasementEvidence
		
		Prolog "There is a lot of stuff here, haphazardly thrown into a pile."
		
		Text QItemEvidenceBasementRubble """
			You fish through the pile of rubish. While you don't find anything
			of use, you do find several old pictures and a damaged necklace. One
			of the pictures is a post-mortem photograph. You recognize it
			as the woman in the photo where you found the candle. Her corpse is
			properly dressed and arranged in a lifelike pose. The same three
			people--Elias, Sarah, and {c:EventChosenInvestigator}--are standing 
			behind her looking grim.

			Gain the {c:QItemEvidenceBasementRubble} Unique Item, then discard
			this Search token.
		"""
		
		Remove TokenSearchBasementEvidence
	
		foundEvidenceBasement = true
		foundEvidenceCount = foundEvidenceCount + 1
		Exit
	End Page SearchEvidence
	
	Page SearchTrapdoor
		Not Visible
		Triggered By @SearchBasementTrapdoor
		
		Prolog """
			The stack of boxes is piled nearly to your hat. Now that you're
			looking more closely, you can see the many footprints in the dust.
		"""
		Button "Search"
		
		Remove TokenBasementWall, TokenSearchBasementTrapdoor
		Remove TokenDungeonCaveWall
		Add TokenExploreDungeonCaveViaBasement!
		
		Text """
			You move a few boxes and in a couple of minutes, you find it: the
			door from the journal. You spend a few more minutes clearing the 
			way to the door. Discard this Search token
			and the wall, then place an Explore token as indicated.
		"""
		
		Exit
	End Page SearchTrapdoor
End Book Basement